docs {
  Creates a course and assigns course setup tabs in `tabs`.
  You can also send per-tab initial content in `tabData`.
  Example: `tabData.course_info` for first-tab details during create.

  Before running this request, run these lookup requests once:
    - list-streams-lookup (sets `disciplineId`)
    - list-study-levels-lookup (sets `studyLevelId`)
    - list-program-types-lookup (sets `programTypeId`)
    - create-campus or list-campuses (sets `campusId`)

  Course tabs for create flow (14):
    course_info, admission_policy, placements, fees, financial_aid,
    student_housing, exam_policy, faculty, review, library,
    clubs_associations, alliance, other_courses_offered, demo_graphics

  College-only static tabs (not sent in create-course):
    college_overview, student_code_of_conduct, happenings,
    institutions_across_world, commute

  If `tabs` is omitted, backend applies all 14 course tabs by default.
  `tabData` is fully dynamic JSON per tab key.
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 201 || res.status === 200) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data && data.data.id) {
      bru.setEnvVar("courseId", data.data.id);
    }
  }
}
